    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Traditional three bedroom cottage in peaceful and spectacular setting with circa 9 acres of land. Beautiful views overlooking Sruwaddacon Bay which opens out to the Atlantic Ocean.\r\n\r\nSet in an exceptionally peaceful and picturesque coastal location overlooking the spectacular Sruwaddacon Bay with the Atlantic Ocean just beyond, this traditional cottage set on circa 9 acres (Folio MY5210) offers endless potential.\r\n\r\nThe cottage comprising of a front porch, entrance hallway, kitchen/dining room, three bedrooms and a bathroom, is in need of complete refurbishment, but offers purchasers an exciting opportunity to transform and modernise the accommodation to create a wonderful permanent home, holiday retreat or coastal escape. This property would also most likely qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant.\r\n\r\nThis wonderfully unspoilt part of north Mayo is renowned for its rugged coastline, stunning beaches, dramatic scenery and strong sense of community, making it particularly appealing to those wishing to escape the pace of modern life and embrace a quieter way of living. The surrounding countryside and coastline provide an abundance of opportunities for outdoor pursuits including coastal walks, hill walking, fishing, and cycling.\r\n\r\nThe property is conveniently positioned just a short walk/cycle from Pullathomas national school and church, with many other amenities including a health centre, GAA pitch, playground, sports centre and shop all closeby. Barnatra is approximately eight minutes' drive, while the larger towns of Belmullet and Bangor Erris are both less than 20 minutes away, offering a good range of shops, schools, cafés, restaurants and essential services. \r\n\r\nFurther afield, the historic towns of Killala, Crossmolina and Ballina are accessible within approximately an hour's drive, providing additional shopping, leisure and cultural amenities. \r\n\r\nExcellent mobile phone coverage in the area, together with access to rural broadband services makes this an ideal home for those wishing to work remotely with stunning surroundings.\r\n\r\nBrimming with potential, this property offers an exciting opportunity for someone to put their own stamp on a home in an exceptional setting, with the added benefit of the circa 9 acres of surrounding land."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Front Porch \r\n2.04m (6'8\") x 0.95m (3'1\")\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway \r\n0.28m (11\") x 8.95m (29'4\")\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining \r\n7.48m (24'6\") x 3.61m (11'10\")\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 \r\n3.32m (10'11\") x 2.3m (7'7\")\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 \r\n3.67m (12'0\") x 2.33m (7'8\")\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 \r\n5.31m (17'5\") x 4.18m (13'9\")\r\n\r\nBathroom \r\n2.66m (8'9\") x 2.65m (8'8\")"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Traditional three-bedroom cottage brimming with potential\r\nCirca 9 acres of surrounding land – Folio MY5210\r\nMost likely qualify for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant\r\nFrontage onto Sruwaddacon Bay\r\nLocated along the Wild Atlantic Way\r\nNational school & church within walking/cycling distance\r\nCoastal walks, stunning beaches & several natural attractions in close proximity\r\nClose to amenities in Barnatra, Kilcomman, Glenamoy, Belmullet & Bangor Erris\r\nLarger towns of Killala, Ballina, & Crossmolina less than a 1-hour drive away"
